+## 2026-08-21 — Estate spawning canon: STRICT cluster placement for director-spawned terminals (supersedes the 08-17 "NOT 100%" mix at the default)
+
+- **Origin (user ruling 2026-08-21, ~23:5xZ play session, verbatim anchors):** *"not so great looking topology"* — the 5.12 soft bias (750‰ attach coin, cap 8) leaves "too many strays and estates that read as noise"; the user wants *"most nodes NEXT TO each other, like an estate, and after ~5 nodes a NEW area elsewhere, leaving routing room between sections."*
+- **Decision — the STRICT estate doctrine (shape (a) of the briefing):** every growth spawn is exactly one of two classes — **ATTACH** (an eligible cluster exists → the candidate sits within `radius_tiles` of a member — the estate extends) or **SEED** (no eligible cluster → a fresh area at ≥ `new_area_seed_tiles` from every live terminal, still in the outward-from-mesh annulus). The delta over 5.12: bias default 750→**1000** (strict; the coin-miss branch remains as a data option at < 1000), cap 8→**5** (the "after ~5 nodes" band), NEW `new_area_seed_tiles` = **10** (2× the adjacency radius — visually distinct sections on the 40×30 map, within the era-3 connect span 18 for E31), plus two zero-draw rejection predicates that close the stray classes the strict audit exposes:
+  1. **`growth_attach_radius_ok`** — the attach candidate must sit within the *Euclidean* radius of its anchor member. The 5.12 compass draw's diagonal directions placed candidates at up to dist×√2 (5.7–7.1 tiles) from the anchor — outside the adjacency radius, inside the seed floor: the exact third class the ruling deletes (measured pre-fix: 7 of 19 growth.dem spawns were strays (37%) under the strict lens).
+  2. **Anchor is a LIVE TERMINAL only** — the derived cluster view leaves dead slots' `id` at 0, which collides with cluster 0's id (the fixture residential at slot 0): a raw id match counted non-terminals (routers) as members and anchored "attaches" on a ROUTER — another stray source.
+- **Shape consequence (documented, not accidental):** with the attach dist range [min_sep, radius] = [4, 5], every diagonal compass draw lands at dist×√2 ≥ 5.66 > radius 5 and rejects pre-E31 — accepted attach geometry is CARDINAL-ONLY, so estates read as **compact crosses** (the ~50% per-attempt budget burn on diagonal draws is the known, deterministic cost).
